Storage Classes
===============
Standard.
Infrequent.
Reduced Redundancy storage.
Glacier.

Standard,
we can maintain object which are going to be accessed frequently [high availablity and better performance].
standard is the default storage class for the objects that we upload into S3 bucket.

Infrequent access,
It is designed for data that is access less frequently but still needs to be retrievable quickly when needed.

Reduced redundancy storage,
We can maintain non critical and reproducable data.

Glacier,
We can maintain archival data - data which we don't use often like application log files.

Object Life Cycle
=================
we can define object life cycle so that AWS will take care of transferring objects from one storage class to another storage class.

