CIDR - Classless Internet Domain Network
========================================
We need to define network [IP range] while creating VPC.

We need to define network range in the form of CIDR.
CIDR is a method for allocating IP addresses and its routing to Private Networks.

CIDR Block must be a valid IPv4 CIDR.

Public IPs  will be given/assigned to resources by ISPs - Internet Service Providers.

Subnet mask
===========
We can calculate how many IPs will be available for Private Network based on subnet mask.

192.168.0.0/20

/16
/17 is a subnet mask.
Subnet mask range must be between 16 to 28

192.168.0.0/26

 32-n	32-26	8 
2		2		2 = 2*8=256

192.168.0.0/16

 32-n	32-15	16 
2		2		2 = 2*16=65536

We get 65535 Private IPs using subnet mask.

192.168.0.0
