Subnet - Sub Network.
=====================
We divide VPC [network] into multiple sub networks.

We can create 'N' number of subnets.
We can create resources like ec2 servers and load balancers etc within subnets.

Types of Subnets
Public subnet.
Private Subnet.

Public subnet.
Subnet which will have an access to internet called as Public subnet.
Servers in public subnet can access interne and we can reach servers also from internet.

Private
subnet which will not have an access to internet called as private subnet.
Servers in private subnet cannot access intnernet and we cannot reach servers also from internet.

Load Balancer servers can be created in public subnets.
Application servers and database servers can be created in private subnets to secure applications.

Internet Gateway
================
Internet Gateway can be associated with VPC.
IGW is a Virtual router in AWS which will enable Internet connectivty to VPC.
IGW will be attached to Subnet in Route table. 1:05:31minutes

1 IGW can be attached to only 1 VPC.

Route Tables
============
Route tables routes network traffic to resources in a VPC.

Subnets which are associated with internet gateway in a route table called as public subnets.
Subnets which are not associated with internet gateway in route table called as private subnets.

NAT Gateway
===========
We create NAT Gateway,
when private servers created in private subnets needs access to internet to download software packages.

NAT Gateway is managed by AWS.

Security Groups
===============
Security Group is a firewal at server/instance level.
We need to allow whatever Ports whatevers sources we need, by default is Deny.
Security Group is stateful.
which means whatever port we're allowed in Inbound Automatically will be allowed [opened] in outbound.

NACL - Network access control list
==================================
It is firewall at subnet level.
NACL will be created automatically whens subnets are created.
NACL supports allow rules and deny rules.
NACL is stateless,
Which means whatever port we're are allowed in inbound are not automatically will be allowed [opened] in outboud.

